      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There are proven ways to loosen, stabilize, or even dissolve plaque already present, rather than just managing its speed of growth. Statins, for example, can encourage the body to remove existing plaque from artery walls and prevent new particles from depositing in the first place. Additionally, specific diets and medications can encourage the body to repair damaged vessel linings, effectively keeping the \"pipes\" open and flexible to prevent further hardening. Therefore, with consistent medical and lifestyle intervention, you can actively reverse the process and significantly reduce your future heart risk.",
